A Trump Account is "a new type of individual retirement account" held for the exclusive benefit of the child, even though a parent, guardian, or other authorized individual opens it, according to the [IRS](https://www.irs.gov/trumpaccounts). A kids savings account is different, because it is often a joint or custodial account with a parent listed as co-owner. The money in a Trump Account stays locked until January 1 of the year the child turns 18, and the [Trump Account rules guide](/guides/trump-account-rules/) covers the account's other limits.